      "id": "4dcab899413c213079e0de468743c790",
      "title": "It\u2019s Time to Settle With Russia",
      "summary": "In October, U.S. President Donald Trump sold his eleventh-hour deal to secure diesel from Russian President Vladimir Putin\u2014pausing sanctions that his own administration had imposed\u2014as a boon for the negotiations to end the war in Ukraine. The arrangement, he wrote on Truth Social, was intended to keep Russia at \u201cthe bargaining table.\u201d Of course, it was always obvious to observers that the gambit had as much or more to do with bolstering the U.S. economy and stemming a massive victory for the Democrats in this month\u2019s midterm elections, and in that, it failed.Cynics have grounds for questioning all of Trump\u2019s moves when it comes to Russia and Ukraine. He clearly dislikes Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky and shows a marked preference for illiberal leaders, especially those willing to give him easy wins. Still, a stopped clock can be right twice a day. And concessions such as the fuel deal are exactly what might move Russia and Ukraine closer to peace, even if they are not wholly motivated by public-spiritedness.",
